Log every contact event and every physics tick.                          (SIM-27)

MEASUREMENT ONLY. REQUIRES 0008, 0009 and 0010 applied first -- it is cut against that exact
stack (it extends 0008's gate enum and sits beside 0009's edit in onCollision).

WHY. With 0008 + 0010 deployed, the split window produced NO log lines at all: no contact
(A/B/C), no grounded tick (D), no release (E). Gate D only fires while the body is grounded, so
silence there means "not grounded" -- and silence in A/B/C means the engine was never told about
a contact. Silence is not evidence, and this ticket has already twice read it as if it were.

  gate=G-TICK  EVERY physics tick, grounded or not: grounded flag, z, vz, and whether the
               stored collision info says has_collided. Unconditional, so a descent through
               the surface produces a visible trace instead of an absence.
  gate=F-HIT   every Unreal hit event reaching PawnSimApi::onCollision (10 Hz throttle):
               count, object name, impact z, actor z, and the normal as UE reported it.

WHAT IT DECIDES. If F is silent through the descent while G shows the body falling, Unreal is
not generating hit events for whatever is stopping the actor, and no change inside
FastPhysicsEngine can help -- the fix belongs in how the pawn is moved or how that geometry
responds. If F fires and G shows the body still descending, the events are arriving and being
discarded, and the discard is findable.

Read with:  docker logs sim-unreal 2>&1 | grep -E "gate=[FG]"

--- a/Unreal/Plugins/AirSim/Source/AirLib/include/physics/FastPhysicsEngine.hpp
+++ b/Unreal/Plugins/AirSim/Source/AirLib/include/physics/FastPhysicsEngine.hpp
